var e={file:`2026-1027-texts-alaska-tt.docx`,date:`2026-10-27`,key:`10-27`,paragraphs:932,blocks:[{k:`heading`,p:[0,0],text:`OCTOBER 27 (celebrated NOVEMBER 9 for churches on the Julian Calendar)`},{k:`heading`,p:[1,1],text:`Righteous Olga of Kwethluk, Wonderworker, Matushka of All Alaska`},{k:`note`,p:[3,3],text:`Note: The Holy Synod of the Orthodox Church in America appoints that a Vigil-rank commemoration, presented here, be celebrated in the Diocese of Alaska, in churches named in honor of St. Olga, and in churches where her relics may be found. A Doxology-rank commemoration, presented in a separate document, is appointed for other churches.`},{k:`heading`,p:[5,5],text:`(At Small Vespers)`},{k:`heading`,p:[6,6],text:`"Lord I Call..." Tone 1`},{k:`text`,p:[8,13],text:`[Lord], I call upon Thee, [hear] me! | [Hear] me, O Lord! | [Lord], I call upon Thee, [hear] me! | Re[ceive] the [voice] of my prayer, | when I [call] up[on] Thee! // [Hear] [me], O Lord!`,n:6,head:`"Lord I Call..." Tone 1`,pointed:!0},{k:`text`,p:[15,19],text:`Let my [prayer] arise | in Thy sight as [in]cense, | and [let] the lifting [up] of my hands | be an [eve]ning [sac]rifice! // [Hear] [me], O Lord!`,n:5,head:`"Lord I Call..." Tone 1`,pointed:!0},{k:`note`,p:[21,21],text:`V. (4) From the morning watch until night, from the morning watch, let Israel hope on the Lord!`},{k:`heading`,p:[23,23],text:`Tone 1 (O all-praised martyrs)`},{k:`text`,p:[25,30],text:`O [right]eous Mother [Ol]ga, | though thy relics were yet covered by the [fro]zen earth, | thy [lov]ing prayers [warmed] the world. | Uncovering thy [pre]cious [rel]ics | and [bow]ing before them in veneration, we en[treat] thee: // Pray always to Christ for those who suffer and [sor]row.`,n:6,head:`Tone 1 (O all-praised martyrs)`,pointed:!0},{k:`note`,p:[32,32],text:`V. (3) For with the Lord there is mercy and with Him is plenteous redemption, and He will deliver Israel from all his iniquities.`},{k:`text`,p:[34,34],text:`(Repeat: “O righteous Mother Olga…”)`,n:1,head:`Tone 1 (O all-praised martyrs)`},{k:`note`,p:[35,35],text:`V. (2) Praise the Lord, all nations! Praise Him, all peoples!`},{k:`text`,p:[37,42],text:`O [gen]erous Mother [Ol]ga, | thy holy relics are treasured in the village of [Kweth]luk, | yet thy [lov]ing intercessions work wonders in [ev]ery place. | Marveling at the great [love] that a[bides] in thee, | we [bend] the knees of our heart in [prayer] to thee: // Beseech Christ that our souls may [yet] be saved.`,n:6,head:`Tone 1 (O all-praised martyrs)`,pointed:!0},{k:`note`,p:[44,44],text:`V. (1) For His mercy is confirmed on us, and the truth of the Lord endures forever.`},{k:`text`,p:[46,49],text:`O [wise] Mother [Ol]ga, | though we no longer know thee ac[cord]ing to the flesh, | yet be[hold]ing thine icon we see the beauty of thy [spir]it. | Perceiving the Light and Wisdom of God dwelling in thee, we [sup]pli[cate] thee:// Entreat Christ to grant conversion to the erring and to us true con[tri]tion.`,n:4,head:`Tone 1 (O all-praised martyrs)`,pointed:!0},{k:`note`,p:[51,51],text:`Glory to the Father, and to the Son, and to the Holy Spirit;`},{k:`heading`,p:[53,53],text:`Tone 6`},{k:`text`,p:[55,62],text:`O blessed [Ol]ga, | thou art the joy of [Kweth]luk | and the glory of the Church in A[las]ka. | O kind-hearted and holy [ma]tushka, | together with all the saints intercede for thy [child]ren, | the faithful in Alaska and through[out] the world, | that we may obtain from [Christ] our true God // healing for our souls and also great [mer]cy.`,n:8,head:`Tone 6`,pointed:!0},{k:`note`,p:[64,64],text:`now and ever, and unto ages of ages. Amen.`},{k:`heading`,p:[66,66],text:`Tone 6 (Theotokion)`},{k:`text`,p:[68,72],text:`O Theo[to]kos, | thou art the true vine who hast put forth the [Fruit] of life. | We pray to thee, O [La]dy: | “Pray, together with the holy a[pos]tles, // that He may be [mer]ciful to our souls.”`,n:5,head:`Tone 6 (Theotokion)`,pointed:!0},{k:`heading`,p:[74,74],text:`(At Small Vespers)`},{k:`heading`,p:[75,75],text:`Aposticha`},{k:`heading`,p:[77,77],text:`Tone 2 (O House of Ephratha)`},{k:`text`,p:[79,83],text:`Orthodox A[las]ka, | cradle of [sanc]tity, | A[mer]ica’s Northern [Hol]y Land: | adorn the [tem]ple // where blessed Olga’s [rel]ics lie.`,n:5,head:`Tone 2 (O House of Ephratha)`,pointed:!0},{k:`note`,p:[85,85],text:`V. Rejoice in the Lord, O you righteous; praise befits the just. (Ps. 32:1)`},{k:`text`,p:[87,91],text:`Kuskokwim and [Yu]kon, | land of A[las]ka, | [all] the Church of North A[mer]ica: | join in the feast of righteous [Ol]ga, // the new wonder[wor]ker.`,n:5,head:`Tone 2 (O House of Ephratha)`,pointed:!0},{k:`note`,p:[93,93],text:`V. Blessed are all those who fear the Lord, who walk in His ways. (Ps. 127:1)`},{k:`text`,p:[95,99],text:`Holy Mother [Ol]ga, | matushka of all A[las]ka, | who workest [won]ders the world [ov]er: | ceaselessly [in]tercede // for all faithful Orthodox [Christ]ians.`,n:5,head:`Tone 2 (O House of Ephratha)`,pointed:!0},{k:`note`,p:[101,101],text:`Glory to the Father, and to the Son, and to the Holy Spirit;`},{k:`note`,p:[102,102],text:`now and ever, and unto ages of ages. Amen.`},{k:`heading`,p:[104,104],text:`Tone 2 (Theotokion)`},{k:`text`,p:[106,110],text:`Ever-virgin [Moth]er, | [mys]tical Bride, | [Daught]er of the [King]: | pray for us, O Virgin Theo[to]kos, // beloved of the Most Holy [Trin]ity.`,n:5,head:`Tone 2 (Theotokion)`,pointed:!0},{k:`heading`,p:[114,114],text:`(At Great Vespers)`},{k:`heading`,p:[115,115],text:`"Lord I Call..." Tone 7`},{k:`text`,p:[117,122],text:`[Lord], I call upon Thee, [hear] me! | [Hear] me, O Lord! | [Lord], I call upon Thee, [hear] me! | Re[ceive] the [voice] of my prayer, | [when] I call up[on] Thee! // [Hear] [me], O Lord!`,n:6,head:`"Lord I Call..." Tone 7`,pointed:!0},{k:`text`,p:[124,128],text:`[Let] my [prayer] arise | in Thy [sight] as [in]cense, | and [let] the lifting [up] of my hands | be an [eve]ning [sac]rifice! // [Hear] [me], O Lord!`,n:5,head:`"Lord I Call..." Tone 7`,pointed:!0},{k:`note`,p:[130,130],text:`V. (8) Out of the depths I cry to Thee, O Lord. Lord, hear my voice!`},{k:`heading`,p:[132,132],text:`Tone 7 Idiomela`},{k:`text`,p:[134,140],text:`[Come], O ye faithful from many [na]tions! | Come, O ye [child]ren from every tribe and clan on A[las]kan soil! | Let us all [hast]en to blessed Matushka Olga, our holy [help]er, | for she [al]ways welcomes hungry children or [those] in need. | She [qui]etly takes away our pain and [suf]fering, | she [humb]ly opens to us the way to [peace] and hope, // by directing us to the worship of the Holy Trinity, one in essence and undi[vid]ed.`,n:7,head:`Tone 7 Idiomela`,pointed:!0},{k:`note`,p:[142,142],text:`V. (7) Let Thine ears be attentive to the voice of my supplications!`},{k:`text`,p:[144,144],text:`(Repeat: “Come, O ye faithful…”)`,n:1,head:`Tone 7 Idiomela`},{k:`note`,p:[146,146],text:`V. (6) If Thou, O Lord, shouldst mark iniquities, Lord, who could stand? But there is forgiveness with Thee.`},{k:`text`,p:[149,155],text:`To[day] the villages of Alaska rejoice in this [hol]y feast, | having [gath]ered around thee, O Mother, with [faith] and love, | for in thy [pres]ence, we discover we are children of the Cre[a]tor. | In thy [calm]ness, we encounter the [Prince] of Peace. | [Pray] for us, Árrsamquq, that we may love God and [neigh]bor | through self-[sac]rifice, humility and [con]stant prayer, // following thy holy example, O woman [fav]ored of God.`,n:7,head:`Tone 7 Idiomela`,pointed:!0},{k:`note`,p:[157,157],text:`V. (5) For Thy Name’s sake I wait for Thee, O Lord. My soul has waited for Thy word; my soul has hoped on the Lord.`},{k:`text`,p:[159,159],text:`(Repeat: “Today the villages of Alaska…”)`,n:1,head:`Tone 7 Idiomela`},{k:`note`,p:[161,161],text:`V. (4) From the morning watch until night, from the morning watch, let Israel hope on the Lord!`},{k:`text`,p:[163,169],text:`To[day] we celebrate a woman of great [hol]iness, | our [bless]ed Mother Olga, matushka of all A[las]ka, | re[vealed] by the Creator as a person in the [like]ness of God, | full of com[pass]ion, mercy, and un[fail]ing love. | Con[tin]ue, O holy Olga, to intercede for the broken-[heart]ed, | up[lift] the despondent and those who [feel] alone, // for we all have thee as our conso[la]tion from the Lord.`,n:7,head:`Tone 7 Idiomela`,pointed:!0},{k:`note`,p:[171,171],text:`V. (3) For with the Lord there is mercy and with Him is plenteous redemption, and He will deliver Israel from all his iniquities.`},{k:`text`,p:[173,180],text:`To[day] we celebrate the glorifi[ca]tion | of an A[las]kan-born woman of un[wav]ering faith, | our [bless]ed Mother Olga, matushka of those living on A[las]kan lands, | the [boast] of Kwéthluk, the wealth of the Kúskokwim and Yúkon [riv]ers. | Through [thee], Árrsamquq, God’s glory is revealed in humility and [qui]etness. | O [hum]ble Yúp’ik handmaiden, teach us patience and long[suf]fering. | [Grant] that we may learn to [hold] our tongue, // reserving it to give glory to God Who is [won]drous in His saints.`,n:8,head:`Tone 7 Idiomela`,pointed:!0},{k:`note`,p:[182,182],text:`V. (2) Praise the Lord, all nations! Praise Him, all peoples!`},{k:`text`,p:[184,191],text:`O [hol]y mother of the faithful in A[las]ka, | whose com[pass]ion extends throughout the world to [those] in need: | In [life], thy loving kindness warmed the villages of the [Kusk]okwim, | clothing the [na]ked, feeding the hungry, and en[cour]aging the distressed. | In [glor]y now, thy loving hands restore the [bat]tered and abused, | re[veal]ing to all the new creation possible in [Christ] our Lord, | re[new]ing our youth like the [ea]gle’s // so that our souls may soar to the Kingdom of [Heav]en.`,n:8,head:`Tone 7 Idiomela`,pointed:!0},{k:`note`,p:[193,193],text:`V. (1) For His mercy is confirmed on us, and the truth of the Lord endures forever.`},{k:`text`,p:[195,202],text:`In days of [old], Saint Peter spoke of holy women who [trust]ed in God, | being a[dorned] with ‘a meek and quiet [spir]it.’ | Saint [Ol]ga is such a woman who a[rose] in our days, | whose ex[am]ple teaches us to walk in the [fear] of God | through small [acts] of kindness and expressions of [mod]esty, | by being a [shel]ter for those beset by the effects of evil [ac]tions. | We [thank] thee for thy kindness and [love] towards us. // Pray thou to the merciful God that He may [save] our souls.`,n:8,head:`Tone 7 Idiomela`,pointed:!0},{k:`note`,p:[204,204],text:`Glory to the Father, and to the Son, and to the Holy Spirit;`},{k:`heading`,p:[206,206],text:`Tone 8`},{k:`text`,p:[208,216],text:`Re[joice] today, O faithful of the [Orth]odox Church, | for ye have gained a mighty inter[cess]or before God: | the holy Árrsamquq, matushka of [all] A[las]ka! | A humble woman who teaches us through [kind] words | and leads us by her holy example of [Christ]ian love, | she shelters those in need and cares for them as [her] own [child]ren, | bringing healing and peace to hearts that others have [wound]ed. | Now she stands in prayer before the Most Holy [Trin]ity // asking for the sal[va]tion of our souls.`,n:9,head:`Tone 8`,pointed:!0},{k:`note`,p:[218,218],text:`now and ever, and unto ages of ages. Amen.`},{k:`heading`,p:[221,221],text:`Tone 8 (Theotokion – Dogmatikon)`},{k:`text`,p:[223,230],text:`The [King] of heaven, because of His [love] for man, | appeared on earth and [dwelt] with men. | He took [flesh] from the pure [Vir]gin | and after assuming it, He came [forth] from her. | The Son is one: in two natures, yet one [Per]son. | Proclaiming Him as perfect [God] and [per]fect Man, | we confess [Christ] our God! // Entreat Him, O unwedded Mother, to have [mer]cy on our souls.`,n:8,head:`Tone 8 (Theotokion – Dogmatikon)`,pointed:!0},{k:`heading`,p:[232,232],text:`Old Testament Readings`},{k:`heading`,p:[233,233],text:`Wisdom of Solomon 3:1-9`},{k:`heading`,p:[234,234],text:`Wisdom of Solomon 5:15-6:3`},{k:`heading`,p:[235,235],text:`Wisdom of Solomon 4:7-15`},{k:`heading`,p:[238,238],text:`Litya`},{k:`note`,p:[239,239],text:`(If the rector desires the Litya, following the sticheron to the Patron Saint of the Temple,`},{k:`note`,p:[240,240],text:`these stichera are sung)`},{k:`heading`,p:[242,242],text:`Tone 5`},{k:`text`,p:[244,254],text:`Re[joice], O Saint Olga, our righteous [moth]er, | for thou hast received the traditions of thine [el]ders, | who loved [God] in a pure Orthodox [man]ner, | and thou didst pre[serve] and hand down those tra[di]tions | as a treasure more [pre]cious than gold. | Thine [Orth]odox faith was manifest in thy humble and pious [way] of life, | in thy [love] for thy neighbor and thy [fear] of God. | May that same faith make us humble and [rev]erent, | that we [too] may come to [know] the joys | of [those] who truly love and serve [Christ] the Lord: // through thy holy intercessions and [God’s] great mercy.`,n:11,head:`Tone 5`,pointed:!0},{k:`note`,p:[256,256],text:`Glory to the Father, and to the Son, and to the Holy Spirit;`},{k:`heading`,p:[258,258],text:`Tone 5`},{k:`text`,p:[260,265],text:`A [star] of sanctity shines brightly over the [Kus]kokwim, | bringing hope and comfort to those who re[joice] in its light: | our [bless]ed Mother Olga of [Kweth]luk, | a phy[si]cian of afflictions of soul and [bod]y | and a quick intercessor for [those] in need. // Pray now, O righteous [moth]er, that our [souls] may be saved.`,n:6,head:`Tone 5`,pointed:!0},{k:`note`,p:[267,267],text:`now and ever, and unto ages of ages. Amen.`},{k:`heading`,p:[269,269],text:`Tone 5 (Theotokion)`},{k:`text`,p:[271,276],text:`O pure [Vir]gin Lady Theo[to]kos, | our hope that cannot be [put] to shame, | be our pro[tec]tion and our de[liv]erance | from the [griev]ous trials and tribulations that be[set] us. | Together with holy Olga and [all] the saints, // entreat thy Son and our God that He may pour out upon [us] His rich [mer]cy.`,n:6,head:`Tone 5 (Theotokion)`,pointed:!0},{k:`heading`,p:[278,278],text:`Aposticha`},{k:`heading`,p:[280,280],text:`Tone 4 (Called from on high)`},{k:`text`,p:[282,289],text:`Thou wast given the grace of cures and [heal]ing; | having been faithful in little, thou wast given au[thor]ity over much | To a [wom]an suffering in spirit and op[pressed] by her past, | thou didst outstretch thy [lov]ing arms, | lifting her up and restoring her to [whole]ness and life. | Wherefore, O holy matushka, comforter of the [suf]fering, | we join her in honoring thy holy [mem]ory, // glorifying our God Who is [won]drous in His Saints.`,n:8,head:`Tone 4 (Called from on high)`,pointed:!0},{k:`note`,p:[291,291],text:`V. Rejoice in the Lord, O you righteous; praise befits the just. (Ps. 32:1)`},{k:`text`,p:[293,300],text:`In the remote wilderness of the Alaskan [tun]dra, | great beauty has arisen like the warm [sun] of spring: | Our [bless]ed Mother Árrsamquq, the kind and [mer]ciful, | who brings comfort and healing to [those] in need. | Touching them with her [gen]tle and [lov]ing hands, | looking at them with a calm and [peace]ful gaze, | she reminds them to [fear] not, // for it is the Father’s good pleasure to give them the [King]dom.`,n:8,head:`Tone 4 (Called from on high)`,pointed:!0},{k:`note`,p:[302,302],text:`V. Blessed are all those who fear the Lord, who walk in His ways. (Ps. 127:1)`},{k:`text`,p:[304,311],text:`Mothers who have lost their children while [still] in the womb | turn to thee, O holy midwife of [Kweth]luk, | [ask]ing in prayer that their unborn be pro[tec]ted in thy care | and safely born into the world to give [glor]y to God. | And as once in Kwethluk, so now thou dost [race] un[to] their aid, | caring for them until their [child]ren can be born, | granting them to see the [fruit] of their womb // and through the Virgin Theotokos, peace and great [mer]cy.`,n:8,head:`Tone 4 (Called from on high)`,pointed:!0},{k:`note`,p:[313,313],text:`Glory to the Father, and to the Son, and to the Holy Spirit;`},{k:`heading`,p:[316,316],text:`Tone 4`},{k:`text`,p:[318,324],text:`Without reading any books, thou didst become di[vine]ly wise, | for thou didst read all of Creation as a [book] from God. | The [words] from the divine services so deeply [touched] thy soul, | that thou didst sing by heart all the hymns from [ev]ery feast, | standing with thy sisters and looking towards the icon of the [Moth]er of God. | Thy simple example showed them how to imitate holy [wom]en of old, // by living in piety, modesty, humility, and the [fear] of the Lord.`,n:7,head:`Tone 4`,pointed:!0},{k:`note`,p:[326,326],text:`now and ever, and unto ages of ages. Amen.`},{k:`heading`,p:[328,328],text:`Tone 4 (Theotokion)`},{k:`text`,p:[330,338],text:`Look on the entreaties of thy servants, O [Blame]less One! | Stop all the terrible attacks a[gainst] us, | [free]ing us from every af[flic]tion, | for we have only thee as our sure and firm [an]chor! | Do not let us be put to [shame], O [La]dy, | for we call on thee for our inter[ces]sion! | Hasten to pray for those who [call] in faith: | “Rejoice, O [La]dy, [Help] of all: // the Joy and Shelter and Sal[va]tion of our souls!”`,n:9,head:`Tone 4 (Theotokion)`,pointed:!0},{k:`heading`,p:[341,341],text:`(at Great Vespers)`},{k:`heading`,p:[343,343],text:`Tone 4 Troparion`},{k:`text`,p:[345,351],text:`God has chosen a humble mother from A[las]ka | to be an example for all the [ser]vants of God; | He has given us Saint Olga as a helper in af[flic]tions | and as a guide to leading a life of sacri[fic]ial love. | Therefore we entreat thee, O holy Mother [Ol]ga: | pray that we, thy sinful [child]ren, may be saved // and rejoice with thee in the Kingdom of [Heav]en.`,n:7,head:`Tone 4 Troparion`,pointed:!0},{k:`note`,p:[353,353],text:`Glory to the Father, and to the Son, and to the Holy Spirit,`},{k:`note`,p:[354,354],text:`now and ever, and unto ages of ages. Amen.`},{k:`heading`,p:[356,356],text:`Tone 4 Resurrectional Dismissal Theotokion`},{k:`text`,p:[358,364],text:`The mystery of all e[ter]nity, | unknown even by [An]gels, | through thee, O Theotokos, is revealed to [those] on earth: | God incarnate by union without con[fu]sion. | He voluntarily accepted the [Cross] for us, | by which He resurrected the first-cre[a]ted man, // saving our [souls] from death.`,n:7,head:`Tone 4 Resurrectional Dismissal Theotokion`,pointed:!0},{k:`heading`,p:[367,367],text:`(at Vigil)`},{k:`heading`,p:[369,369],text:`Tone 4 Troparion`},{k:`text`,p:[371,377],text:`God has chosen a humble mother from A[las]ka | to be an example for all the [ser]vants of God; | He has given us Saint Olga as a helper in af[flic]tions | and as a guide to leading a life of sacri[fic]ial love. | Therefore we entreat thee, O holy Mother [Ol]ga: | pray that we, thy sinful [child]ren, may be saved // and rejoice with thee in the Kingdom of [Heav]en.`,n:7,repeat:`twice`,head:`Tone 4 Troparion`,pointed:!0},{k:`heading`,p:[380,380],text:`Tone 4 Troparion to the Theotokos`},{k:`text`,p:[382,386],text:`Rejoice, O Virgin Theo[to]kos, | Mary, full of grace, the [Lord] is with thee! | Blessed art thou among [wo]men, | and blessed is the [Fruit] of thy womb, // for thou hast borne the [Sav]ior of our souls.`,n:5,repeat:`once`,head:`Tone 4 Troparion to the Theotokos`,pointed:!0},{k:`heading`,p:[389,389],text:`(at Matins)`},{k:`heading`,p:[391,391],text:`“God is the Lord…” Tone 4`},{k:`heading`,p:[393,393],text:`Tone 4 Troparion`},{k:`text`,p:[395,401],text:`God has chosen a humble mother from A[las]ka | to be an example for all the [ser]vants of God; | He has given us Saint Olga as a helper in af[flic]tions | and as a guide to leading a life of sacri[fic]ial love. | Therefore we entreat thee, O holy Mother [Ol]ga: | pray that we, thy sinful [child]ren, may be saved // and rejoice with thee in the Kingdom of [Heav]en.`,n:7,head:`Tone 4 Troparion`,pointed:!0},{k:`note`,p:[403,403],text:`Glory to the Father, and to the Son, and to the Holy Spirit,`},{k:`note`,p:[404,404],text:`now and ever, and unto ages of ages. Amen.`},{k:`heading`,p:[406,406],text:`Tone 4 Resurrectional Dismissal Theotokion`},{k:`text`,p:[408,414],text:`The mystery of all e[ter]nity, | unknown even by [An]gels, | through thee, O Theotokos, is revealed to [those] on earth: | God incarnate by union without con[fu]sion. | He voluntarily accepted the [Cross] for us, | by which He resurrected the first-cre[a]ted man, // saving our [souls] from death.`,n:7,head:`Tone 4 Resurrectional Dismissal Theotokion`,pointed:!0},{k:`heading`,p:[416,416],text:`Kathisma Hymns (following the first reading of the Psalter)`},{k:`heading`,p:[418,418],text:`Tone 6 (The angelic powers)`},{k:`text`,p:[420,425],text:`When a woman distraught by at[tacks] from her peers | hastened to the Church to pray for [guid]ance from the Lord, | Saint Olga appeared in answer to her prayer, instructing her [first] to pray: | “Lord, hold not this sin against them, for they know [not] what they do.” | And then to proclaim, “Christ is [ris]en!” // Truly risen Lord, [glo]ry to Thee!`,n:6,head:`Tone 6 (The angelic powers)`,pointed:!0},{k:`note`,p:[427,427],text:`Glory to the Father, and to the Son, and to the Holy Spirit,`},{k:`note`,p:[428,428],text:`now and ever, and unto ages of ages. Amen.`},{k:`heading`,p:[429,429],text:`Tone 6 (Theotokion)`},{k:`text`,p:[431,438],text:`The apostle Thomas [came] to thy tomb | expecting to find [thee] in the grave, | but thou hadst been taken to heaven in soul and [bod]y | and enthroned as Queen of cre[a]tion. | Interceding together with righteous Olga and [all] the saints, | pray that we may be freed from our deadly [pass]ions. | O Theotokos, Mother of our [King] and our God, // [glor]y to thee.`,n:8,head:`Tone 6 (Theotokion)`,pointed:!0},{k:`heading`,p:[440,440],text:`Kathisma Hymns (following the second reading of the Psalter)`},{k:`heading`,p:[442,442],text:`Tone 2 (When Thou didst descend)`},{k:`text`,p:[444,448],text:`When a [moth]er was distraught at her child’s [ill]ness, | O blessed Olga, in response to her [prayer] thou didst appear, | re[veal]ing that her son’s pure soul would soon be received by the [hands] of God | and causing her to cry [out] with great faith: // “O Source of life eternal, Christ our [God], [glor]y to Thee!”`,n:5,head:`Tone 2 (When Thou didst descend)`,pointed:!0},{k:`note`,p:[450,450],text:`Glory to the Father, and to the Son, and to the Holy Spirit,`},{k:`note`,p:[451,451],text:`now and ever, and unto ages of ages. Amen.`},{k:`heading`,p:[453,453],text:`Tone 2 (Theotokion)`},{k:`text`,p:[455,459],text:`When thou [gav]est birth to the Timeless One, O Theo[to]kos, | thou didst open for us a way to e[ter]nity. | Now inter[cede] for us sinners, O blessed [Vir]gin, | helping us to redeem the time, for the days are [e]vil. // O Mother of Life everlasting and protectress of [Christ]ians, [glor]y to thee!`,n:5,head:`Tone 2 (Theotokion)`,pointed:!0},{k:`heading`,p:[461,461],text:`Polyeleos`},{k:`heading`,p:[463,463],text:`Magnification`},{k:`text`,p:[465,469],text:`We magnify thee, | O holy and righteous Mother Olga, | and we honor thy holy memory, | O healer of those in afflictions | and loving intercessor before the merciful God.`,n:5,head:`Magnification`},{k:`note`,p:[470,470],text:`V. I waited patiently for the Lord, and He was attentive unto me and heard my supplication.`},{k:`note`,p:[471,471],text:`V. He set my feet upon a rock and ordered my steps aright.`},{k:`note`,p:[472,472],text:`V. I saw the Lord always before me, for He is at my right hand, that I may not be moved.`},{k:`note`,p:[473,473],text:`V. Let all Thy works praise Thee, O Lord.`},{k:`note`,p:[474,474],text:`V. Let Thy saints bless Thee.`},{k:`note`,p:[475,475],text:`V. Know also that the Lord hath made wondrous His holy one.`},{k:`note`,p:[476,476],text:`V. He labored forever and shall live unto the end.`},{k:`note`,p:[477,477],text:`V. The Lord preserves the souls of His saints.`},{k:`note`,p:[478,478],text:`V. The saints shall boast in glory and shall rejoice upon their beds.`},{k:`note`,p:[479,479],text:`V. Precious in the sight of the Lord is the death of His saints.`},{k:`note`,p:[480,480],text:`V. Sing unto the Lord, O ye saints of His, and give thanks at the remembrance of His holiness.`},{k:`note`,p:[481,481],text:`Glory to the Father, and to the Son, and to the Holy Spirit,`},{k:`text`,p:[482,482],text:`now and ever, and unto ages of ages. Amen.`,n:1,head:`Magnification`},{k:`heading`,p:[484,484],text:`Kathisma Hymns (following the Polyeleos)`},{k:`heading`,p:[486,486],text:`Tone 5 (Let us, the faithful, praise and worship the Word)`},{k:`text`,p:[488,493],text:`[Come], let us learn of our blessed Mother [Ol]ga, | that we may be grateful in all things to the Holy [Trin]ity, | Who [feeds] even the [birds] of the air, | for with [hum]ble kindness she embraced all, [far] and near; | no one at her door was a [stran]ger, // and none went away with[out] a [gift] from her hand.`,n:6,head:`Tone 5 (Let us, the faithful, praise and worship the Word)`,pointed:!0},{k:`note`,p:[495,495],text:`Glory to the Father, and to the Son, and to the Holy Spirit,`},{k:`note`,p:[496,496],text:`now and ever, and unto ages of ages. Amen.`},{k:`heading`,p:[499,499],text:`Tone 5 (Theotokion)`},{k:`text`,p:[501,506],text:`We de[light] to magnify thy mysteries, O Theo[to]kos, | who didst conceive thy Creator in thine ever-[vir]gin womb | and gavest [birth] to the Infinite in a [cave] of earth. | We [glor]ify thee as the beginning of our sal[va]tion, | the gateway of God, our entrance into e[ter]nity, // the [Moth]er of our Resur[rec]tion.`,n:6,head:`Tone 5 (Theotokion)`,pointed:!0},{k:`heading`,p:[508,508],text:`Tone 4 Prokeimenon`},{k:`text`,p:[510,510],text:`I waited patiently for the Lord, / and He was attentive unto me and heard my supplication. (Ps. 39:1)`,n:1,head:`Tone 4 Prokeimenon`},{k:`note`,p:[512,512],text:`V. He set my feet upon a rock and ordered my steps aright. (Ps. 39:3)`},{k:`text`,p:[514,514],text:`Let everything that breathes praise the Lord!`,n:1,head:`Tone 4 Prokeimenon`},{k:`note`,p:[516,516],text:`V. Praise God in His sanctuary! Praise Him in His mighty firmament! (Ps. 150:1)`},{k:`heading`,p:[518,518],text:`Gospel`},{k:`text`,p:[519,519],text:`(74) Matthew 18:1-11`,n:1,head:`Gospel`},{k:`heading`,p:[521,521],text:`Tone 6 Post-Gospel Sticheron`},{k:`text`,p:[523,536],text:`As our Lord was moved to compassion upon seeing the [mul]titudes, | so wast thou moved to compassion upon seeing [those] in need. | As the [seas]ons changed, | so did the labor of thy com[pass]ionate hands. | In the renewal of [spring]time, | thou didst feed the villagers with what was [caught] in the wilds. | In the warmth of [sum]mer, | thou didst preserve for them netfuls of fish for the freezing [months] to come. | In the confinement of fall and [win]ter, | thy handiwork would bring them [warmth] in the cold. | At every season and [ev]ery hour, | thou didst fulfill the com[mand]ments of thy Lord: | now living forever beyond all [sea]sons and times, // intercede for us, O holy Mother Olga, before the Sus[tain]er of all life.`,n:14,head:`Tone 6 Post-Gospel Sticheron`,pointed:!0},{k:`heading`,p:[539,539],text:`The Canon`},{k:`heading`,p:[541,541],text:`Tone 2 Ode 1 – Heirmos`},{k:`text`,p:[543,547],text:`In the days of old a mighty force | destroyed all the host of Pharaoh in the deep; | but when the Word became flesh, | the most glorious Lord blotted out all the wickedness of sin, | for gloriously has He been glorified.`,n:5,head:`Tone 2 Ode 1 – Heirmos`},{k:`text`,p:[549,549],text:`R. Righteous Mother Olga, pray to God for us.`,n:1,head:`Tone 2 Ode 1 – Heirmos`},{k:`text`,p:[551,551],text:`In the days of old God gave Aaron to Moses as a support for his stammering tongue; now do Thou Thyself, O Word, support my tongue and provide it a word, accustomed as it is to stuttering the words of sin, that I may praise Olga, whom Thou hast glorified.`,n:1,head:`Tone 2 Ode 1 – Heirmos`},{k:`text`,p:[553,553],text:`R. Righteous Mother Olga, pray to God for us.`,n:1,head:`Tone 2 Ode 1 – Heirmos`},{k:`text`,p:[555,555],text:`Throughout the ages God has raised up holy women as mothers in the Faith to be helpers of the Christian people, intercessors for believers, and examples of righteous conduct for all, and in these latter days He added to their ranks Saint Olga, in whom He is glorified.`,n:1,head:`Tone 2 Ode 1 – Heirmos`},{k:`text`,p:[557,557],text:`R. Righteous Mother Olga, pray to God for us.`,n:1,head:`Tone 2 Ode 1 – Heirmos`},{k:`text`,p:[559,559],text:`Through His saints—Herman and Innocent, Yakov and Juvenaly—the Lord brought His saving Gospel to the native peoples of Alaska. The saints’ preaching and teaching, as a sowing of salvation, fell on good soil, and now from that soil springs forth righteous Olga, that the Lord may ever be glorified.`,n:1,head:`Tone 2 Ode 1 – Heirmos`},{k:`note`,p:[561,561],text:`Glory to the Father, and to the Son, and to the Holy Spirit,`},{k:`note`,p:[562,562],text:`now and ever, and unto ages of ages. Amen.`},{k:`text`,p:[564,564],text:`From the root of Jesse blossomed forth life, salvation, and joy for the world when the Virgin Bride gave birth in the flesh to the eternal Word by Whom all things were made, while the angels in heaven cried: “In the highest has He been glorified.”`,n:1,head:`Tone 2 Ode 1 – Heirmos`},{k:`heading`,p:[566,566],text:`Tone 2 Ode 3 – Heirmos`},{k:`text`,p:[568,570],text:`The desert, the barren Church of the gentiles, | has blossomed like a lily at Thy coming, O Lord, | in which my heart has been established.`,n:3,head:`Tone 2 Ode 3 – Heirmos`},{k:`text`,p:[572,572],text:`R. Righteous Mother Olga, pray to God for us.`,n:1,head:`Tone 2 Ode 3 – Heirmos`},{k:`text`,p:[574,574],text:`The tundra, the Yukon-Kuskokwim Delta, the Orthodox Christian Yup’ik people, have shaped a new vessel of holiness, blessed Matushka Olga, as a meet offering to Christ.`,n:1,head:`Tone 2 Ode 3 – Heirmos`},{k:`text`,p:[576,576],text:`R. Righteous Mother Olga, pray to God for us.`,n:1,head:`Tone 2 Ode 3 – Heirmos`},{k:`text`,p:[578,578],text:`Orthodox Alaska, the northern Holy Land, has brought forth the righteous Olga, a new intercessor for the faithful throughout the world.`,n:1,head:`Tone 2 Ode 3 – Heirmos`},{k:`text`,p:[580,580],text:`R. Righteous Mother Olga, pray to God for us.`,n:1,head:`Tone 2 Ode 3 – Heirmos`},{k:`text`,p:[582,582],text:`The Church in America, a tender shoot planted by Thy right hand, O Lord, celebrates her new saint, Olga, who wafts Thy healing to the four corners of the world.`,n:1,head:`Tone 2 Ode 3 – Heirmos`},{k:`note`,p:[584,584],text:`Glory to the Father, and to the Son, and to the Holy Spirit,`},{k:`note`,p:[585,585],text:`now and ever, and unto ages of ages. Amen.`},{k:`text`,p:[587,587],text:`The all-holy Lady who alone gave birth to God in the flesh now stands before Him praying for the Christian people, and accompanying her in prayer is blessed Olga.`,n:1,head:`Tone 2 Ode 3 – Heirmos`},{k:`heading`,p:[589,589],text:`Kathisma Hymns`},{k:`heading`,p:[591,591],text:`Tone 4 (Joseph marveled)`},{k:`text`,p:[593,599],text:`The faithful marvel when they behold the great and many [won]ders | accomplished by thy prayers, O holy [Ol]ga, | and they glorify God Who hath given thee such [pow]er | to comfort the suffering and correct [those] who err. | Through thee we experience the all-powerful love of God, [cry]ing out: | “The prayers of righteous Olga of [Kweth]luk // are a balm and ointment for [wound]ed souls.”`,n:7,head:`Tone 4 (Joseph marveled)`,pointed:!0},{k:`note`,p:[601,601],text:`Glory to the Father, and to the Son, and to the Holy Spirit,`},{k:`note`,p:[602,602],text:`now and ever, and unto ages of ages. Amen.`},{k:`heading`,p:[604,604],text:`Tone 4 (Theotokion)`},{k:`text`,p:[606,613],text:`Wise men came from afar to [wor]ship the Child | who lay in thine arms, O all-holy Theo[to]kos, | for the Creator and Pro[vid]er of all | willed to be born of thee as Savior and De[liv]erer. | Shepherds who abode nearby were also summoned by angelic [her]alds | to witness Immortality clothed in [mor]tal flesh, | for from thee, O most holy [Lad]y, // Christ came forth to redeem me and raise me [up] from my fall.`,n:8,head:`Tone 4 (Theotokion)`,pointed:!0},{k:`heading`,p:[616,616],text:`Tone 2 Ode 4 – Heirmos`},{k:`text`,p:[618,623],text:`Thou didst come from a Virgin, | not an ambassador nor an Angel | but the Lord Himself incarnate, | and Thou didst save my entire human nature; | therefore, I cry out to Thee: | Glory to Thy power, O Lord.`,n:6,head:`Tone 2 Ode 4 – Heirmos`},{k:`text`,p:[625,625],text:`R. Righteous Mother Olga, pray to God for us.`,n:1,head:`Tone 2 Ode 4 – Heirmos`},{k:`text`,p:[627,627],text:`As a worthy matushka, O Saint Olga, thou wast a helpmeet to thy husband and a true and loving mother to all the people of Kwethluk, generous with thy goods and wise in thy counsels.`,n:1,head:`Tone 2 Ode 4 – Heirmos`},{k:`text`,p:[629,629],text:`R. Righteous Mother Olga, pray to God for us.`,n:1,head:`Tone 2 Ode 4 – Heirmos`},{k:`text`,p:[631,631],text:`Thy hands were ever busy with works of love, O blessed Mother, and the works of thy hands supplied warm clothing to thy family, to other priests and parishes, and to all in want and in need.`,n:1,head:`Tone 2 Ode 4 – Heirmos`},{k:`text`,p:[633,633],text:`R. Righteous Mother Olga, pray to God for us.`,n:1,head:`Tone 2 Ode 4 – Heirmos`},{k:`text`,p:[635,635],text:`The Lord became man on account of His all-embracing love, and through thy generosity, O Olga, obedient handmaiden of the Savior, thou didst manifest the all-encompassing and self-emptying love of Christ the Lord.`,n:1,head:`Tone 2 Ode 4 – Heirmos`},{k:`note`,p:[637,637],text:`Glory to the Father, and to the Son, and to the Holy Spirit,`},{k:`note`,p:[638,638],text:`now and ever, and unto ages of ages. Amen.`},{k:`text`,p:[640,640],text:`From thee, O Virgin Mother, the Lord, bowing the heavens, came down for our salvation, and now at thy prayers, and the prayers of thy handmaid, Olga, He parts the heavens once more to work wonders for His faithful people.`,n:1,head:`Tone 2 Ode 4 – Heirmos`},{k:`heading`,p:[642,642],text:`Tone 2 Ode 5 – Heirmos`},{k:`text`,p:[644,649],text:`O Enlightenment of those who lie in darkness, | Salvation of the despairing, | Christ my Savior, | early in the morning I come before Thee, the King of peace. | Illumine me with Thy radiance, | for I know no other god but Thee.`,n:6,head:`Tone 2 Ode 5 – Heirmos`},{k:`text`,p:[651,651],text:`R. Righteous Mother Olga, pray to God for us.`,n:1,head:`Tone 2 Ode 5 – Heirmos`},{k:`text`,p:[653,654],text:`Faithful to the traditions of thine Orthodox Christian Yup’ik elders and the holy tradition of the Russian Orthodox Church brought to Alaska by the saints, thou wast a gentle bulwark of piety and humble reverence, O righteous Mother. | R. Righteous Mother Olga, pray to God for us.`,n:2,head:`Tone 2 Ode 5 – Heirmos`},{k:`text`,p:[656,656],text:`O compassionate correction of those who err, O patient mother of thy children, O blessed Matushka Olga, we come before thee in our weakness and pain, O tender guide, and we ask thee to show us the way to healing in Christ, our true God and Savior.`,n:1,head:`Tone 2 Ode 5 – Heirmos`},{k:`text`,p:[658,658],text:`R. Righteous Mother Olga, pray to God for us.`,n:1,head:`Tone 2 Ode 5 – Heirmos`},{k:`text`,p:[660,660],text:`Great are the accomplishments of faith, and the accomplishments of thy humble faith in Christ and His Church have greatly magnified thee as a new wonderworker, through whom Christ grants us swift cures, saving reproofs, and a mighty ally in spiritual battle.`,n:1,head:`Tone 2 Ode 5 – Heirmos`},{k:`note`,p:[662,662],text:`Glory to the Father, and to the Son, and to the Holy Spirit,`},{k:`note`,p:[663,663],text:`now and ever, and unto ages of ages. Amen.`},{k:`text`,p:[665,665],text:`O dawn of our redemption and Mother of the Light, healer of those sick with passions, O Theotokos, we come before thee and ask thy prayers, and also the prayers of thy handmaid, Olga, for we recognize these intercessions as our only hope.`,n:1,head:`Tone 2 Ode 5 – Heirmos`},{k:`heading`,p:[667,667],text:`Tone 2 Ode 6 – Heirmos`},{k:`text`,p:[669,671],text:`Whirled about in an abyss of sins, | I call on the unfathomable abyss of Thy compassion: | Lead me up out of corruption, O God!`,n:3,head:`Tone 2 Ode 6 – Heirmos`},{k:`text`,p:[673,673],text:`R. Righteous Mother Olga, pray to God for us.`,n:1,head:`Tone 2 Ode 6 – Heirmos`},{k:`text`,p:[675,675],text:`Afflicted with grief and pain, suffering women encounter the all-abundant love of God by thy prayers, O Olga, and out of their desolation they behold the beauty of His healing.`,n:1,head:`Tone 2 Ode 6 – Heirmos`},{k:`text`,p:[677,677],text:`R. Righteous Mother Olga, pray to God for us.`,n:1,head:`Tone 2 Ode 6 – Heirmos`},{k:`text`,p:[679,679],text:`Beset with sorrow and losing hope, barren couples are granted children by thy prayers, O Olga, and the families of the Orthodox rejoice in God’s saints.`,n:1,head:`Tone 2 Ode 6 – Heirmos`},{k:`text`,p:[681,681],text:`R. Righteous Mother Olga, pray to God for us.`,n:1,head:`Tone 2 Ode 6 – Heirmos`},{k:`text`,p:[683,683],text:`Gripped by confusion and despair, the lost children of Holy Church are found by thy prayers, O Olga, and led back to the true worship of God.`,n:1,head:`Tone 2 Ode 6 – Heirmos`},{k:`note`,p:[685,685],text:`Glory to the Father, and to the Son, and to the Holy Spirit,`},{k:`note`,p:[686,686],text:`now and ever, and unto ages of ages. Amen.`},{k:`text`,p:[688,688],text:`Tossed to and fro by the lashing winds of despondency and pride, I call upon thee, O good and beneficent Lady: Most holy Theotokos, save us!`,n:1,head:`Tone 2 Ode 6 – Heirmos`},{k:`heading`,p:[692,692],text:`Tone 8 Kontakion`},{k:`text`,p:[694,700],text:`Guided by the [heav]enly [light] and touched by Christ’s rich [mer]cy, | thy loving [hands] heal the [wounds] of those [hurt] in the past. | Thy soft voice en[cour]ages [all] to remain [faith]ful to God, | for the e[ter]nal [Lord] will give the steadfast a [crown] of life. | O holy [Moth]er [Ol]ga, visit us with love and reas[sur]e us, | that we may ac[cept] whatever [cross] we must bear as chosen by the [mer]ciful God // and that, through thy [prayers], we do the [will] of God for the sal[va]tion of our souls.`,n:7,head:`Tone 8 Kontakion`,pointed:!0},{k:`heading`,p:[702,702],text:`Ikos`},{k:`text`,p:[704,704],text:`As the matushka of Kwethluk, thy hands were always busy with works of love, and now as a holy mother for all the Orthodox faithful, thou art ever occupied with prayer for those who stand in need of help or healing. Witnessing the love of Christ revealed in thy life and wonders, O righteous Olga, we thy children greet thee with these words of praise: “Rejoice, O Saint Olga, boast of Kwethluk and the Kuskokwim, praise of the Yup’ik people, new wonderworker of Alaska and all the world!” Taught by thine example and strengthened by thy supplications, may we always do the will of God for the salvation of our souls.`,n:1,head:`Ikos`},{k:`heading`,p:[707,707],text:`Tone 2 Ode 7 – Heirmos`},{k:`text`,p:[709,712],text:`When the golden idol was worshipped in the plain of Dura, | Thy three children despised the godless order. | Thrown into the fire, they were bedewed and sang: | “Blessed art Thou, O God of our fathers.”`,n:4,head:`Tone 2 Ode 7 – Heirmos`},{k:`text`,p:[714,714],text:`R. Righteous Mother Olga, pray to God for us.`,n:1,head:`Tone 2 Ode 7 – Heirmos`},{k:`text`,p:[716,716],text:`Singing by heart the hymns of the Lord’s Passion and Pascha, O righteous Mother, thou didst show thyself to be a true initiate of the Mysteries of the Lord’s life and sufferings, a true child of Holy Church, and a true daughter of the God of our fathers.`,n:1,head:`Tone 2 Ode 7 – Heirmos`},{k:`text`,p:[718,718],text:`R. Righteous Mother Olga, pray to God for us.`,n:1,head:`Tone 2 Ode 7 – Heirmos`},{k:`text`,p:[720,720],text:`Since thou didst daily die to thyself through tireless works of self-emptying love, O blessed Olga, at the time of thine exodus thou didst pass through the stormy waves of death and dost even now partake of the light of Christ’s Resurrection.`,n:1,head:`Tone 2 Ode 7 – Heirmos`},{k:`text`,p:[722,722],text:`R. Righteous Mother Olga, pray to God for us.`,n:1,head:`Tone 2 Ode 7 – Heirmos`},{k:`text`,p:[724,724],text:`Because thou didst put the passions to death in thy flesh, O holy matushka, now thy sacred relics stream with life and power. For those who approach them with faith, they are a pure spring streaming with the sweet dew of God’s wonders.`,n:1,head:`Tone 2 Ode 7 – Heirmos`},{k:`note`,p:[726,726],text:`Glory to the Father, and to the Son, and to the Holy Spirit,`},{k:`note`,p:[727,727],text:`now and ever, and unto ages of ages. Amen.`},{k:`text`,p:[729,729],text:`The clamorous instruments of the world call my heart to worship idols of gold and iron, but I flee to thy help, O Virgin. Though I am burning in temptation’s fire, nevertheless I sing: Blessed art thou among women, O Mother of God!`,n:1,head:`Tone 2 Ode 7 – Heirmos`},{k:`heading`,p:[731,731],text:`Tone 2 Ode 8 – Heirmos`},{k:`text`,p:[733,737],text:`The God Who came down to the children | of the Hebrews in the fiery furnace, | and who transformed the flame into dew, | do all ye works praise as Lord, | and exalt above all forever.`,n:5,head:`Tone 2 Ode 8 – Heirmos`},{k:`text`,p:[739,739],text:`R. Righteous Mother Olga, pray to God for us.`,n:1,head:`Tone 2 Ode 8 – Heirmos`},{k:`text`,p:[741,741],text:`The God Who descended into Hades and ended the reign of death, and Who commanded the storms and seas, called upon the south wind to melt the ice and snow at the time of our blessed mother’s funeral. Exalt Him above all forever.`,n:1,head:`Tone 2 Ode 8 – Heirmos`},{k:`text`,p:[743,743],text:`R. Righteous Mother Olga, pray to God for us.`,n:1,head:`Tone 2 Ode 8 – Heirmos`},{k:`text`,p:[745,745],text:`Alaskans came from the Yukon and Kuskokwim region and beyond, O righteous Mother, to sing thee to thy rest, and the sudden spring-like weather was a sign that thou hast entered into the joy of thy Lord’s Paschal victory. Exalt Him above all forever.`,n:1,head:`Tone 2 Ode 8 – Heirmos`},{k:`text`,p:[747,747],text:`R. Righteous Mother Olga, pray to God for us.`,n:1,head:`Tone 2 Ode 8 – Heirmos`},{k:`text`,p:[749,749],text:`At the time of the uncovering of thy sacred relics, O blessed Olga, the Lord, Who casts forth ice as morsels and gives snow like wool, did quiet the blizzard that raged so that pilgrims could attend thy holy uncovering. Exalt Him above all forever.`,n:1,head:`Tone 2 Ode 8 – Heirmos`},{k:`note`,p:[751,751],text:`Let us bless the Father, the Son, and the Holy Spirit, the Lord,`},{k:`note`,p:[752,752],text:`now and ever, and unto ages of ages. Amen.`},{k:`text`,p:[754,754],text:`The Lamb Who was slain before the foundation of the world, Who is the Word and Wisdom of the Father, born in time of the most holy Virgin Mother and crucified under Pontius Pilate, do all ye works praise as Lord, and exalt above all forever.`,n:1,head:`Tone 2 Ode 8 – Heirmos`},{k:`text`,p:[756,756],text:`We praise, bless and worship the Lord, singing and exalting Him throughout all ages.`,n:1,head:`Tone 2 Ode 8 – Heirmos`},{k:`heading`,p:[757,757],text:`Tone 2 Ode 9 – Heirmos`},{k:`text`,p:[759,764],text:`The Son of the Father without beginning, | God the Lord, has appeared to us | made flesh of a Virgin, | to give light to what is darkened | and to gather together what is scattered: | therefore we magnify the all-praised Theotokos.`,n:6,head:`Tone 2 Ode 9 – Heirmos`},{k:`text`,p:[766,766],text:`R. Righteous Mother Olga, pray to God for us.`,n:1,head:`Tone 2 Ode 9 – Heirmos`},{k:`text`,p:[768,768],text:`Thy relics repose in Kwethluk, at the temple of Saint Nicholas, O Mother, but in the Spirit thou dost traverse the orb of the world, working wonders for those who call upon thee with faith and love. Therefore we magnify the God Who so glorified thee.`,n:1,head:`Tone 2 Ode 9 – Heirmos`},{k:`text`,p:[770,770],text:`R. Righteous Mother Olga, pray to God for us.`,n:1,head:`Tone 2 Ode 9 – Heirmos`},{k:`text`,p:[772,772],text:`Thou art the healer of those who suffered abuse and tragedy, the mother of children separated from their parents, the swift aid of women in hard labor, the comfort of all those wounded in heart and soul, and we magnify thee as a new wonderworker like Nicholas.`,n:1,head:`Tone 2 Ode 9 – Heirmos`},{k:`text`,p:[774,774],text:`R. Righteous Mother Olga, pray to God for us.`,n:1,head:`Tone 2 Ode 9 – Heirmos`},{k:`text`,p:[776,776],text:`Thou art the glory of the Yup’ik people, the pride of Kwethluk and all the Kuskokwim, the boast of Alaska, the ornament of Orthodox America, a new North Star in the firmament of Christ’s holy Church. Therefore we magnify thee as our mighty intercessor.`,n:1,head:`Tone 2 Ode 9 – Heirmos`},{k:`note`,p:[778,778],text:`Glory to the Father, and to the Son, and to the Holy Spirit,`},{k:`note`,p:[779,779],text:`now and ever, and unto ages of ages. Amen.`},{k:`text`,p:[781,781],text:`Thou art a chalice brimming with ever-flowing love for us, thy children, O Theotokos most sweet, and Saint Olga is also full of maternal love for us. Therefore we magnify her as the matushka of all Alaska and a universal wonderworker, and thee as the Mother of all right-believing Christians.`,n:1,head:`Tone 2 Ode 9 – Heirmos`},{k:`heading`,p:[783,783],text:`Exapostilarion`},{k:`heading`,p:[785,785],text:`Tone 3 (O Word, Light unaltered)`},{k:`text`,p:[787,792],text:`Today we behold thy virtue as a light, O holy Mother [Ol]ga, | which provides hope and courage in our [dark]est days. | Thou hast [shown] us the light, | the light of Christ that il[lum]ines all, | as thou dost il[lum]ine all // with the light of thy life of [love] and self-[sac]rifice.`,n:6,head:`Tone 3 (O Word, Light unaltered)`,pointed:!0},{k:`note`,p:[794,794],text:`Glory to the Father, and to the Son, and to the Holy Spirit,`},{k:`note`,p:[795,795],text:`now and ever, and unto ages of ages. Amen.`},{k:`text`,p:[797,801],text:`Thou art the sweetness of the angels, O Virgin [Moth]er of the Word; | thou art the protection of the en[tire] world. | Through thee we have [seen] Christ, the Radiance of the [Fath]er, | by the bright overshadowing of the [Spir]it: // deliver us from our [fail]ings and trans[gres]sions.`,n:5,head:`Tone 3 (O Word, Light unaltered)`,pointed:!0},{k:`heading`,p:[803,803],text:`The Praises Tone 1`},{k:`text`,p:[805,808],text:`Let [ev]erything that breathes [praise] the Lord! | Praise the Lord from the [heav]ens! | [Praise] Him in the [high]est! // To Thee, O God, is [due] a song!`,n:4,head:`The Praises Tone 1`,pointed:!0},{k:`text`,p:[810,812],text:`[Praise] Him, all you [An]gels of His! | Praise Him, [all] His hosts! // To Thee, O God, is [due] a song!`,n:3,head:`The Praises Tone 1`,pointed:!0},{k:`note`,p:[814,814],text:`V. Praise Him for His mighty deeds; praise Him according to His exceeding greatness! (Ps. 150:2)`},{k:`heading`,p:[816,816],text:`Tone 1 (Joy of the Heavenly Hosts)`},{k:`text`,p:[818,822],text:`O [hol]y and humble Mother [Árr]samquq, | in whom God is [won]drous, | we re[joice] in the beauty of thy [hol]iness, | and we do not hide our [love] and de[vo]tion to thee. // Lovingly remember us before the Cre[a]tor.`,n:5,head:`Tone 1 (Joy of the Heavenly Hosts)`,pointed:!0},{k:`note`,p:[824,824],text:`V. Praise Him with trumpet sound; praise Him with lute and harp! (Ps. 150:3)`},{k:`text`,p:[826,829],text:`O [hol]y and kind-hearted Mother [Ol]ga, | whom God has glorified on account of thy humility and self-[sac]rifice, | inter[cede] for us who are [weak] of will, // and lovingly remember us before the Cre[a]tor.`,n:4,head:`Tone 1 (Joy of the Heavenly Hosts)`,pointed:!0},{k:`note`,p:[831,831],text:`V. Praise Him with timbrel and dance; praise Him with strings and pipe!`},{k:`note`,p:[832,832],text:`(Ps. 150:4)`},{k:`text`,p:[834,837],text:`O [hol]y and gentle Mother [Ol]ga, | who dost know our life and our many temp[ta]tions, | we [nev]ertheless desire to walk in thy pious [foot]steps. // Lovingly remember us before the Cre[a]tor.`,n:4,head:`Tone 1 (Joy of the Heavenly Hosts)`,pointed:!0},{k:`note`,p:[839,839],text:`V. Praise Him with sounding cymbals; praise Him with loud clashing cymbals! Let everything that breathes praise the Lord! (Ps. 150:5)`},{k:`text`,p:[841,845],text:`[Pray] for thy [child]ren, | O blessed matushka of [Kweth]luk, | for [though] we are unworthy of God’s [mer]cy, | we know that thy [moth]erly love [nev]er fails: // lovingly remember us before the Cre[a]tor.`,n:5,head:`Tone 1 (Joy of the Heavenly Hosts)`,pointed:!0},{k:`note`,p:[847,847],text:`Glory to the Father, and to the Son, and to the Holy Spirit,`},{k:`heading`,p:[849,849],text:`Tone 6`},{k:`text`,p:[851,857],text:`O Maker and Redeemer, [Christ] our God, | help us to follow the example of Thy humble handmaiden, [Ol]ga, | the holy matushka from [Kweth]luk, | by being open-hearted, generous, [lov]ing, and kind. | Remember us when Thou comest in Thy [King]dom, | deliver us from the enemies of the [Orth]odox Faith, // and make us participants in Thine uncreated [glor]y.`,n:7,head:`Tone 6`,pointed:!0},{k:`note`,p:[859,859],text:`now and ever, and unto ages of ages. Amen.`},{k:`heading`,p:[861,861],text:`Tone 6 (Theotokion)`},{k:`text`,p:[863,872],text:`My Maker and Redeemer, [Christ] the Lord, | came forth from thy womb, O all-[pure] one: | by being clothed with me, he freed Adam from the [an]cient curse. | Wherefore, O Theo[to]kos, | to thee, the true Mother of God and [Vir]gin, | we, together with Saint Olga of A[las]ka, | unceasingly cry out with the angel's [greet]ing: | “Rejoice, O [full] of grace! | Rejoice, O [La]dy, // Protection, Shelter, and Sal[va]tion of our souls!”`,n:10,head:`Tone 6 (Theotokion)`,pointed:!0},{k:`heading`,p:[873,873],text:`(at the Divine Liturgy)`},{k:`note`,p:[875,875],text:`At the Verses on the Beatitudes, we sing four troparia from Ode 3 and four troparia from Ode 6 of the Canon.`},{k:`heading`,p:[877,877],text:`Tone 4 Troparion`},{k:`text`,p:[879,885],text:`God has chosen a humble mother from A[las]ka | to be an example for all the [ser]vants of God; | He has given us Saint Olga as a helper in af[flic]tions | and as a guide to leading a life of sacri[fic]ial love. | Therefore we entreat thee, O holy Mother [Ol]ga: | pray that we, thy sinful [child]ren, may be saved // and rejoice with thee in the Kingdom of [Heav]en.`,n:7,head:`Tone 4 Troparion`,pointed:!0},{k:`heading`,p:[887,887],text:`Tone 8 Kontakion`},{k:`text`,p:[889,895],text:`Guided by the [heav]enly [light] and touched by Christ’s rich [mer]cy, | thy loving [hands] heal the [wounds] of those [hurt] in the past. | Thy soft voice en[cour]ages [all] to remain [faith]ful to God, | for the e[ter]nal [Lord] will give the steadfast a [crown] of life. | O holy [Moth]er [Ol]ga, visit us with love and reas[sur]e us, | that we may ac[cept] whatever [cross] we must bear as chosen by the [mer]ciful God // and that, through thy [prayers], we do the [will] of God for the sal[va]tion of our souls.`,n:7,head:`Tone 8 Kontakion`,pointed:!0},{k:`heading`,p:[897,897],text:`Tone 4 Prokeimenon`},{k:`text`,p:[899,899],text:`God is wondrous in His saints, / the God of Israel. (Ps. 67:35a)`,n:1,head:`Tone 4 Prokeimenon`},{k:`note`,p:[901,901],text:`V. Bless God in the churches, the Lord, O you who are of Israel’s fountain!`},{k:`note`,p:[902,902],text:`(Ps. 67:27)`},{k:`heading`,p:[903,903],text:`Epistle`},{k:`text`,p:[904,904],text:`(208) Galatians 3:26-29`,n:1,head:`Epistle`},{k:`heading`,p:[907,907],text:`Tone 1`},{k:`text`,p:[908,908],text:`Alleluia, Alleluia, Alleluia!`,n:1,head:`Tone 1`},{k:`note`,p:[910,910],text:`V. The salvation of the righteous is of the Lord, and He is their defender in the time of affliction. (Ps. 36:40)`},{k:`note`,p:[912,912],text:`V. The Lord shall help them and deliver them, for they have placed their hope on Him. (Ps. 36:41)`},{k:`heading`,p:[914,914],text:`Gospel`},{k:`text`,p:[915,915],text:`(21) Mark 5:24-34`,n:1,head:`Gospel`},{k:`heading`,p:[917,917],text:`Communion Hymn`},{k:`text`,p:[919,920],text:`Rejoice in the Lord, O you righteous; praise befits the just! (Ps. 32:1) | Alleluia, Alleluia, Alleluia!`,n:2,head:`Communion Hymn`},{k:`heading`,p:[924,924],text:`Prayer to Righteous Olga of Kwethluk, Wonderworker,`},{k:`heading`,p:[925,925],text:`Matushka of All Alaska`},{k:`text`,p:[927,928],text:`O blessed Mother, Saint Olga, matushka of all Alaska, new wonderworker, thou wast in all things a faithful handmaiden of the Lord and His most pure Mother, meek and humble, and now for this cause thou art great in the Kingdom, and thy prayers have authority over much. Therefore, visit us, thy children, with thy supplications, O righteous Olga of Kwethluk, and pray that we may keep the Orthodox faith whole and inviolate, just as we have received it from Christ our God, the very Word of the Father, and from His all-laudable Apostles, and from all our holy fathers, elders, and teachers who have come before. Inspired by thy love, we marvel at thine example, and desire to imitate thy great generosity and faithfulness. O pious Mother, pray that we may obtain reverence; O loving Mother, pray that we may be strengthened in the practice of generosity. O humble Mother, pray that we may gain blessed simplicity, an undivided attention to fulfilling the Gospel. O faithful Mother, pray that we may, before the end, understand our sinfulness and attain to true repentance, confessing our faults, shedding blessed tears of sorrow for our many transgressions against God and neighbor, and amending our crooked way of life. | O Saint Olga, matushka of all Alaska and great wonderworker for the Orthodox faithful throughout the world, never cease in thy loving prayers for us, thy children, and intercede that we may always receive healing in soul and body, forgetting about the past and racing to stretch out our hands to the things that lie ahead, so that, by the great and rich and inexpressible mercy of God, which we experience through thy holy intercessions, we may attain to the Kingdom where thou now dwellest with the most holy Theotokos and all the saints in the unfading light of divine love: the Kingdom of the Father and of the Son and of the Holy Spirit, to Whom we render all thanks and glory, now and ever and unto endless ages of ages. Amen.`,n:2,head:`Matushka of All Alaska`},{k:`note`,p:[931,931],text:`Prepared by the Department of Liturgical Music and Translations, Orthodox Church in America.`}]};export{e as default};